## Favorite Labs This Semester

### Lab 1 – "Hello World"
One of my favorite labs this semester was our very first lab, **Lab 1**. This was my first time actually coding something that wasn't on paper. The thrill of figuring out what to do and eventually doing it correctly brought me so much enjoyment and satisfaction. The simple code just to say "Hello World" seemed so complicated when we first started, and I never knew it would lead to coding much more advanced things like handling colors and calling lists.

### Lab 9 – Spell Checker
Another lab I really enjoyed was **Lab 9**, where we coded a spell checker program that checks a file for any misspelled words and prints them out. I enjoyed this lab because it helped me understand how to use vectors, command sizes, and how to work with lines in a file. I also learned to use variables like `ele`, and how I can name them anything I want. It was fascinating to see how flexible programming can be.

### Lab 11 – State Population Density
**Lab 11** was another lab I found really enjoyable. We were given a file containing a table of U.S. states and their population densities. Our task was to pick a state and find out which one is the densest. I had a great time with this lab because it taught us how to access a file, and how to retrieve specific rows and columns from the data to use in our code.

